## Phase 4 — Router Cleanup ([rag.py](file:///Users/siddhanttomar/development/flutter_projects/brain_dump/brain-dump/backend/app/api/routers/rag.py))

Currently the router passes `db: Session` into `rag_engine.index_text` and [delete_document](file:///Users/siddhanttomar/development/flutter_projects/brain_dump/brain-dump/backend/app/services/rag_engine.py#312-323). After the refactor:
- Routers no longer pass [db](file:///Users/siddhanttomar/development/flutter_projects/brain_dump/brain-dump/backend/app/core/database.py#22-28) to RAG functions
- `rag_engine` async wrappers ([async_index_text](file:///Users/siddhanttomar/development/flutter_projects/brain_dump/brain-dump/backend/app/services/rag_engine.py#1062-1076), [async_retrieve_context](file:///Users/siddhanttomar/development/flutter_projects/brain_dump/brain-dump/backend/app/services/rag_engine.py#1032-1046)) talk to the MCP client
- The `SessionLocal()` manual session management in [async_retrieve_context](file:///Users/siddhanttomar/development/flutter_projects/brain_dump/brain-dump/backend/app/services/rag_engine.py#1032-1046), [async_search_brain](file:///Users/siddhanttomar/development/flutter_projects/brain_dump/brain-dump/backend/app/services/rag_engine.py#1048-1060), and [async_index_text](file:///Users/siddhanttomar/development/flutter_projects/brain_dump/brain-dump/backend/app/services/rag_engine.py#1062-1076) goes away

---

## Key Design Decisions to Confirm

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Decision 1: In-process vs. sidecar**
> The plan above goes with a sidecar service. An alternative is to keep the MCP server as an **in-process Python module** (no HTTP, just function calls) and still get the clean separation without the network overhead. This is simpler to deploy and avoids httpx latency, but sacrifices independent scalability and the ability to use the server as a true MCP tool from other clients.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Decision 2: BM25 cache placement**
> The BM25 in-memory index currently lives in [rag_engine.py](file:///Users/siddhanttomar/development/flutter_projects/brain_dump/brain-dump/backend/app/services/rag_engine.py). After the refactor, `fetch_all_for_user` data comes from the MCP server. The BM25 cache (and its invalidation) should stay in [rag_engine.py](file:///Users/siddhanttomar/development/flutter_projects/brain_dump/brain-dump/backend/app/services/rag_engine.py) — it's an orchestration concern, not a storage concern. This means BM25 cache invalidation still happens on the `rag_engine` side, which is correct.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Decision 3: Phasing**
> We can do this progressively: Phase 1 is the MCP server (new service, zero app changes). Phase 2 is wiring the client into [rag_engine.py](file:///Users/siddhanttomar/development/flutter_projects/brain_dump/brain-dump/backend/app/services/rag_engine.py) one function at a time, testing after each. No big-bang rewrite required.

---

## What We Are NOT Changing

- [models.py](file:///Users/siddhanttomar/development/flutter_projects/brain_dump/brain-dump/backend/app/models/models.py) — [BrainEmbedding](file:///Users/siddhanttomar/development/flutter_projects/brain_dump/brain-dump/backend/app/models/models.py#50-57) stays for Alembic history
- [docker-compose.yml](file:///Users/siddhanttomar/development/flutter_projects/brain_dump/brain-dump/backend/docker-compose.yml) `postgres` service — no changes to the DB itself
- The Flutter app — zero changes
- The FastAPI router signatures — no API contract changes
- The chunking, BM25, RRF, and re-ranking logic in [rag_engine.py](file:///Users/siddhanttomar/development/flutter_projects/brain_dump/brain-dump/backend/app/services/rag_engine.py)

